      "min_break_pct": 0.1,
      "min_break_atr": 0.25,
      "level_kinds": {
        "note": "1.5.0 (AFP-02): a LEVEL_BREAK alert is deduplicated per symbol, side (support / resistance) and level kind, never per level value: support and resistance are re-anchored to every completed minute close, so a key holding the value produced a new alert every cycle (124 of 280 stored alerts repeated a symbol and side inside the 1800 s cooldown). The kind comes from the level's basis (first matching prefix, else default): a break of a daily level (previous day or week, N-day range, daily SMA) is a different condition from a break of an intraday one (session, swing, VWAP, volume profile, option strike), so each may alert once per cooldown.",
        "default": "intraday",
        "prefixes": {"previous_day": "daily", "previous_week": "daily", "range_": "daily", "sma_": "daily"}
      },
      "max_reference_age_seconds": 900,
      "note_max_reference_age_seconds": "1.5.0 (AFP-01): levels are tested for a break only while they describe the current market. Levels anchored to a minute close older than this many seconds (the first cycle after a restart or data gap anchors them to a bar 12-20 h old), levels flagged reference.stale, and levels of a decision past its expires_at are ignored: no alert and brief level state UNKNOWN. 900 s = the 300 s analysis cadence plus the last completed minute and a slow cycle."
    },
